# DBiz Intelligence Plane — line-ending and diff policy.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. Developers work on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) while CI runs ubuntu-latest. Without
# a policy, the same file checks in with different line endings depending on who committed it, which
# produces whole-file phantom diffs and makes review and `git blame` unreliable. This file fixes the
# normalised form IN THE REPOSITORY to LF while leaving each developer's working copy alone.
#
# This changes no file content: every path below is already stored with LF, so applying this policy is
# a no-op for the current tree. It constrains future commits, not existing ones.

# Default: detect text, store it as LF in the repository. Working-copy endings stay platform-native.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ── Explicit text types ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.ts       text eol=lf
*.tsx      text eol=lf
*.js       text eol=lf
*.mjs      text eol=lf
*.cjs      text eol=lf
*.json     text eol=lf
*.jsonl    text eol=lf
*.md       text eol=lf
*.yml      text eol=lf
*.yaml     text eol=lf
*.html     text eol=lf
*.css      text eol=lf
*.sh       text eol=lf
*.sql      text eol=lf
*.txt      text eol=lf
.gitignore      text eol=lf
.gitattributes  text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf

# Shell scripts and Dockerfiles MUST be LF even on Windows — CRLF breaks the shebang and RUN lines
# inside a Linux container. Covered above; restated here because it is a correctness rule, not style.

# ── Binary: never normalise, never diff as text ────────────────────────────────
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.tgz  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.eot  binary

# ── Generated / lock files: keep them out of review noise ──────────────────────
# linguist-generated collapses them by default in diffs; they remain fully tracked and diffable.
pnpm-lock.yaml text eol=lf linguist-generated=true
